  set:  # e7cc
    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] 2026-11-01 review (dev 100b6fbb6e): cert-manager analyze_go counts identical to filing (cc=method resolved dst: function 306 all logs.WithResource, struct 11, field 158); alertmanager function 2, type 2. Narrowing: a bare untyped local (y:=get(); y.Helper()) is now guarded (external 0.4); binding shapes seen are pkg.Var.M() (corev1.SchemeGroupVersion.*), an external call result (tmpltext.New(\"\").Option -> repo Option type), and a package whose name differs from its import leaf (go-smtp: smtp.NewServer -> unrelated repo NewServer 0.85). (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFOUND 2026-10-03 while fixing WI-kugap (branch jgstern-agent/fix/kibah, commit 0adbd3fa21 restamps the construct of resolved receiver calls).\n\nA call written on a VALUE (x.F(), call_construct=method) whose receiver the analyzer could not type falls through the ambiguity / visibility / stdlib-interface guards to resolver.lookup(callee_name) with no hint, and the sole repo candidate of that short name is bound whatever its KIND. Go cannot reach a free function, a struct or a type from a value's selector (only a method or a func-typed field), so a function / struct / type dst is wrong by construction.\n\nMeasured on the kibah branch (analyze_go, edges with evidence ast_call, call_construct=method, resolved dst):\n- cert-manager: 306 -> kind function, 11 -> struct, 158 -> field. All 306 function binds are one shape: `corev1.SchemeGroupVersion.WithResource(\"secrets\")` (a method on an EXTERNAL package variable, k8s schema.GroupVersion, absent from library_signatures/go.yaml package_variables) bound to the repo function pkg/logs/logs.go:WithResource.\n- prometheus: 6 function, 312 field. alertmanager: 2 function, 2 type, 78 field. coredns: 23 field.\nBefore WI-kugap these same edges were stamped call_construct=function, which hid the contradiction; the edges themselves predate the branch (dev has the same function binds).\n\nFIX SHAPE (not built): on a value receiver, accept a resolved symbol only of kind method (or a func-typed field: see WI-jalal-lijab-podat-bizor-lovul-fijit-rihor-fuhut for the field half); a function / struct / type hit is not the callee and the call stays unresolved.\n\nNOT MEASURED: how many of the field binds are func-typed fields (WI-jalal's split)."  # e7cc
